      "text": "To find the modulus (or absolute value) of a complex number $a + bi$, we use the formula:\n\\[ |a + bi| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}. \\]\n\nFor the given complex number $\\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\right|$, we can identify $a = \\frac{1}{2}$ and $b = -\\frac{3}{8}$. Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[ \\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\right| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(-\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2}. \\]\n\nCalculating the squares:\n\\[ \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{4}, \\]\n\\[ \\left(-\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2 = \\frac{9}{64}. \\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{9}{64} = \\frac{16}{64} + \\frac{9}{64} = \\frac{25}{64}. \\]\n\nTaking the square root of the sum:\n\\[ \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{64}} = \\frac{5}{8}. \\]\n\nTherefore, the modulus is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{5}{8}}. \\]",
